Author: jeremy <jeremy@3tched.localdomain>
Date:   Thu Aug 20 07:13:29 2026 +0000

    fix(openflow): request all ports in OF1.5 PORT_DESC; degrade static flows
    
    OF1.5 added an ofp15_port_desc_request body that OF1.3 does not have
    (openflow-1.5.h: "All ports if OFPP_ANY"). build_port_desc_request left it
    zero-filled, so it asked for port 0 -- not a valid port. OVS answered with an
    empty list and no error, so every symbolic port name silently failed to
    resolve. Observed on the wire:
    
      OFPST_PORT_DESC request (OF1.5) (xid=0x4): port=0
      OFPST_PORT_DESC reply   (OF1.5) (xid=0x4):      <- empty
    
    Write OFPP_ANY at body[8..12] and correct the stale pad(12) doc comment to the
    real type(2)+flags(2)+pad(4)+port_no(4)+pad(4) layout.
    
    Three further changes so one unresolvable flow cannot take down the datapath:
    
    - Move the static FDB re-assert from step 6c to 5b, ahead of the static-flow
      loop and its barrier. L2 reachability must never be gated on symbolic port
      resolution -- without the pin, actions=NORMAL floods every port.
    - Static-flow loop skips and logs instead of `?`, with a static_skipped
      counter. The plugin declares atomic_operations: false; the previous `?` made
      it all-or-nothing with infinite retry.
    - Barrier OFPT_ERROR warns instead of bail!, and breaks when the error carries
      barrier_xid so a rejected barrier cannot hang the connection.
    
    Adds test_port_desc_request_asks_for_all_ports.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

